      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Quick Start Guide: GridFlow CLI\n\nWelcome to the GridFlow CLI documentation. This guide will walk you through setting up and deploying your first project using GridFlow CLI to ensure a smooth and efficient process.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore getting started, ensure you have the following installed and configured:\n\n1. Docker: Required for running containerized applications.\n2. AWS CLI: Must be pre-configured with the `gridscale-prod` profile for access to GridScale resources.\n\n## Connection Setup\n\nFirstly, authenticate the command-line interface (CLI) to access the GridScale services using the following command:\n\n```\ngridflow auth login --profile gridscale-prod\n```\n\n## Project Initialization\n\nTo initialize a new project, execute the following command, replacing `<project-name>` with the desired name for your project:\n\n```\ngridflow init <project-name>\n```\n\n## Deployment\n\nWith your project initialized, you're ready to start deploying. Deploy your application to the staging environment by running:\n\n```\ngridflow deploy --env staging\n```\n\n## Status Verification\n\nAfter deployment, verify the status of your projects to ensure everything has been deployed correctly by using:\n\n```\ngridflow status\n```\n\nThen check the output to confirm the deployment's success",
      "source": "target",
