      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Comprehensive Quick Start Guide: GridFlow CLI\n\n## Introduction\n\nWelcome to the comprehensive Quick Start Guide for the GridFlow CLI, your essential toolkit for simplifying and streamlining the deployment process in our development workflows. This guide not only provides you with step-by-step instructions but also offers insights that empower you with best practices and a thorough understanding crucial for leveraging GridFlow CLI effectively.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nPrior to using GridFlow CLI, the following software installations and configurations are imperative:\n\n1. **Docker:** A containerization platform that isolates your environment, ensuring a smoother deployment. Make sure it's installed by running `docker --version` in your terminal to get the installed version, which should align with our prescribed container versions.\n\n2. **AWS CLI:** The Global Cloud Automation Software’s command-line interface tool that interacts with services like Amazon Web Services. Pre-configuration of the `gridscale-prod` profile guarantees access only to the GridScale resources corresponding to the production environment, ensuring our deployments are secure and environment-specific.\n\nBefore installing or configuring gridflow, be sure to get the AWS CLI configured with the following command, substituting your access keys accordingly:\n\n```bash\naws configure set default.aws_access_key_id <your_access_key>\naws configure set default",
